From: EglantinePS5
Subject: [PATCH] up: EDEN_UP_BACKX_DRAW fix, only the split's back skips break adds (checker fix to 1005)

Fix to 1005's port of lucastaonline's 865afaa4f3 (#1161), as taken into zortos293/Lichii
5e428570d2 (PR #1586, Zortos (zortos293) with capy-ai).

With EDEN_UP_BACKX_DRAW=1, any thread that called Nx2FastDraw::Serial() became a "reader" whose
breaks skip the locked add once it has bumped the serial since its last read. The GPU thread
draws (and reads the serial in PrepareDraw) before GpuSplit::MaybeStart starts the back; after
that it is the front, reads the serial no more, and so would skip every break after its first for
the rest of the session. A front break between two back draws then leaves the serial unchanged and
the back's next draw takes a stale delta (wrong picture). Now only the thread GpuSplit::BackLoop
marks (the back, the only thread whose draws can be reused: Ineligible::OffBackThread) re-arms in
Serial(); every other thread always adds, as without the switch. Without the split nothing is a
reader. Unset: as before. No translation id input: KEEPS THE STORE.

diff --git a/src/video_core/gpu_split.cpp b/src/video_core/gpu_split.cpp
index 47d5279da1..662e6a61ee 100644
--- a/src/video_core/gpu_split.cpp
+++ b/src/video_core/gpu_split.cpp
@@ -1201,6 +1201,7 @@ size_t GpuSplit::ExecuteCaught(const u64* entry, size_t words) {
 void GpuSplit::BackLoop(std::stop_token stop_token) {
     Common::SetCurrentThreadName("GPUBack");
     on_back_thread = true;
+    VideoCommon::Nx2FastDraw::MarkSerialReaderThread(); // 1006, EDEN_UP_BACKX_DRAW only
     Common::GuestReadThrough::MarkGpuThread(1); // 0900: the front's fault handler knows this thread
     back_running.store(true, std::memory_order_release);
     Common::SetCurrentThreadPriority(Common::ThreadPriority::Critical);
diff --git a/src/video_core/nx2_fast_draw.h b/src/video_core/nx2_fast_draw.h
index 656a8b5383..39203ea384 100644
--- a/src/video_core/nx2_fast_draw.h
+++ b/src/video_core/nx2_fast_draw.h
@@ -181,6 +181,14 @@ inline std::atomic<u32> g_last_break{};
 /// write traps, unmaps) always bump.
 inline thread_local bool t_reads_serial{};
 inline thread_local bool t_serial_bumped{};
+/// 1006: only the split's back may become a reader (GpuSplit::BackLoop sets it). Before the back
+/// starts, the GPU thread (the front later) draws and reads the serial too; marked a reader then,
+/// it would skip its register breaks for the rest of the session (it reads no more), and the
+/// back's next draw would take a stale delta. Unmarked threads always bump, as before.
+inline thread_local bool t_serial_reader_thread{};
+inline void MarkSerialReaderThread() noexcept {
+    t_serial_reader_thread = true;
+}
 
 /// Set once by Maxwell3D's constructor: the 10-second log line will be written
 /// (EDEN_NX2_GPU_PROFILE or EDEN_UP_FAST_DRAW_VERIFY), so Break counts each reason.
@@ -217,7 +225,7 @@ inline void Break(Reason reason, u32 method = 0) {
 /// The thread that draws: what it compares fast draws with (with EDEN_UP_BACKX_DRAW, from then
 /// on its next break bumps the serial again).
 inline u64 Serial() {
-    if (UpBackX::g_draw) [[unlikely]] {
+    if (UpBackX::g_draw && t_serial_reader_thread) [[unlikely]] {
         t_reads_serial = true;
         t_serial_bumped = false;
     }
